3.  We use `http.Get()` to send a GET request to the specified URL. The `Get()` function returns a response and an error. If an error occurs, we print the error and exit.
4.  We check the status code of the response. If it's `http.StatusOK` (200), we print a success message. Otherwise, we print an error message with the status code.
5.  We close the response body using `resp.Body.Close()` to prevent resource leaks, regardless of whether an error occurred or not.

